    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15507" root="رسل" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِرْسَالٌ</span></b>  One <i>who sends the morsel</i> [<i>that he eats</i>]
<i>into his fauces:</i> or <i>who throws forth the branch
from his hand,</i> (O, K,) <i>when he goes in a place
of trees,</i> (O,) <i>in order that he may hurt his companion.</i> (O, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>A short arrow:</i> (S, O:) or
<i>a small arrow.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَسْلٌ</span>, in three
places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَسُولٌ</span>.

  </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
